# OmaleBrandProfile-1 — Enterprise-Grade Upgrade Plan

## Overview

This plan upgrades the **E-WIN ProfileX** SvelteKit 5 + Convex + Firebase application from a functional prototype to a production-ready, enterprise-grade platform. The audit identified **critical security gaps, broken mobile responsiveness, missing routes, Convex backend weaknesses, and UI/design inconsistencies** that must all be resolved.

---

## Critical Findings Summary

> [!CAUTION]
> **Admin and Dashboard routes have ZERO server-side auth protection.** Any user can visit `/admin` and see all applications, service requests, and audit logs without logging in.

> [!WARNING]
> **Google Fonts (Bebas Neue, Space Mono) are never loaded in `app.html`** — they silently fall back to system fonts across the entire UI.

> [!WARNING]
> **Mobile layout is broken** — IAMOnboarding floating stats overflow viewport, Hero image column is fixed-height and clips on small screens, DashboardLayout sidebar doesn't restore scroll, BottomNav is hidden at md but dashboard routes need it.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **`/register/iam`, `/admin/settings`, `/dashboard/profile` are referenced in nav but do not exist as SvelteKit routes.**

---

## Open Questions

1. Should `/register/iam` be a full SvelteKit page (replacing the legacy HTML files in `/static/platforms/`)?
2. Should the light mode theme be a full toggle (stored in localStorage) or system-preference-only?
3. Do you want email notifications (e.g. via Resend/Mailgun) triggered when a service request is submitted?
4. Should Convex queries be paginated, or is a hard limit (e.g. take 200) acceptable for now?
5. Should the Member Dashboard (`/dashboard`) require a completed IAM application (approved status) to access, or just any Firebase login?

